  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/webidl/issues/comments/996224190",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/whatwg/webidl/issues/71#issuecomment-996224190",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/webidl/issues/71",
    "id": 996224190,
    "node_id": "IC_kwDOANeiys47YSy-",
    "user": {
      "login": "bathos",
      "id": 6257356,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjYyNTczNTY=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6257356?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/bathos",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/bathos",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bathos/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bathos/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bathos/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bathos/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bathos/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bathos/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bathos/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bathos/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bathos/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "created_at": "2021-12-16T21:56:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-12-16T22:18:33Z",
    "body": "> Should promise getters be required to use [NewObject]? \r\n\r\nWas this meant to say [SameObject]? [NewObject] is only defined for operations and I assumed this was because that behavior is very problematic in practice for attributes. Neither is permitted by a Promise<T> attribute.\r\n\r\nAlthough there is at least one existing quirk where this doesn't hold (valueAsDate), attribute getters that cause SameValue(foo.bar, foo.bar) to always be false (i.e., with no other code in between) tend to break JS expectations, sometimes catastrophically (e.g. the old Angular diffing algorithm).\r\n\r\n\"Can use [NewObject]\" isn't true for any attribute currently, regardless of its type. [SameObject] does work with attributes but specifically forbids Promise<T> types. AFAIK it's for \"fully permanent\" values, i.e. never changing regardless of application state, not just never changing across consecutive accesses.\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/webidl/issues/comments/996224190/reactions",
