    "created_at": "2021-12-16T23:33:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-12-16T23:33:50Z",
    "body": "> Was this meant to say [SameObject]? [NewObject] is only defined for operations and I assumed this was because that behavior is very problematic in practice for attributes. Neither is permitted by a Promise attribute.\r\n\r\nNo, I meant [NewObject]. (The title of the issue made me think attributes could have [NewObject].) I guess my understanding was overly simplified if even Promise typed attributes can indeed return the same Promise object multiple times. And it makes sense that they can.\r\n\r\nIn that case I think this issue can be closed as obsolete since it sounds like there are no outstanding changes to be made, wrt the title/original topic of this issue. #1077 tracks the issue about unions/objects/etc that was previously raised as a tangent of this issue.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
