    "updated_at": "2021-12-16T23:51:36Z",
    "body": "Both of these extended attributes are a bit odd in that they are \"pure\" annotations describing high level API behavior. They have no corresponding effects in any Web IDL algorithms. They seemingly don't meet Web IDL's own definition for what an extended attribute is because they don't control behaviors that are specific to particular language bindings. That definition is likely just outdated, but like ... if you have found any of this confusing, you're right :)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
