    "created_at": "2021-12-17T20:06:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-12-17T20:06:23Z",
    "body": "That makes sense. The distinction I meant to highlight was that they describe universal properties of the operation/attribute behavior itself. Contrast e.g. PutForwards, which is defined only in terms of ES binding behavior, where any other binding (unless given its own rules for interpretting that EA) just sees a readonly attribute.",
